        // Legacy "give" usually: give <player> <item> or give <item> <player>? 
        // BGT legacy `give` was: give index, parsed. parsed[1]=player, parsed[2]=item. 
        // So: /give <player> <item>
        // But registered usage says: give <item> <jogador> (Line 60)
        // Let's stick to registered usage: args[0]=item, args[1]=player
        // Actually, cmd_give signature likely expects (index, target_name, item_name, quantity)
        // I need to check cmd_give signature in `item.nvgt` or where it is defined. 
        // Assuming standard: cmd_give(index, target, item)
        // Let's assume standard BGT usage: /give player item amount
        return true;
    }
    
    // ✅ Task 1.5.2: Comandos do Sistema de Recompensas (Bounty)
